++Subject: [PATCH 27/67] input: hall: Make the bring-up build usable for
++ diagnosis
++
++Flashing the previous bring-up image showed two problems with it:
++
++ - SELinux still reported Enforcing.  Forcing permissive in selinux_init() is
++   not enough: Android init writes 1 to /sys/fs/selinux/enforce early, and the
++   node is root only, so the kernel cannot be flipped back from adb shell and
++   neither /proc/eebbk_kmsg nor the vendor sysfs nodes can be read.  Ignore
++   writes to that node when CONFIG_BBK_DEBUG_BRINGUP is set, so the bring-up
++   image really does stay permissive.
++
++ - the hall sensors still do not bind, and without the kernel log there is
++   nothing to go on.  Under the same symbol, let an unreadable register or an
++   adapter that does not advertise SMBUS_I2C_BLOCK only warn instead of
++   failing the probe, so one flash both produces the log and gives the driver
++   a chance to bind and report what the sensor actually answers.
++
++The strict, vendor-like checks remain compiled in for every other build: the
++relaxations live in #ifdef CONFIG_BBK_DEBUG_BRINGUP branches.
++
++Signed-off-by: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
