+++From c75936266df22618f7d2ba0770041162c026a599 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+++From: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
+++Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 19:36:43 +0800
+++Subject: [PATCH 03/40] techpack: Build the audio stack and the ADSP loader
+++ into the kernel
+++
+++techpack/Kbuild reads obj-${TECHPACK}, so passing TECHPACK=n compiles only
+++techpack/stub/: the image carries no audio code at all and, above all, no
+++techpack/audio/dsp/adsp-loader.c.  Nothing then binds the "qcom,adsp-loader"
+++device tree node or calls subsystem_get("adsp"), so the ADSP never boots:
+++adsprpcd loops on "Transport endpoint is not connected", no sound card is
+++created and the device freezes on the boot animation.  The vendor copy of that
+++loader cannot substitute for it, being ABI incompatible with this tree.
+++
+++Build with TECHPACK=y (techpack/Kbuild's own default) and add a post-build
+++self-check that the audio stack really landed in Image.gz.
+++
+++Signed-off-by: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
