++From fcdee8c2f2d220654fca1621d78035cb4b8efce7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
++From: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
++Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:43:46 +0800
++Subject: [PATCH 56/67] docs: Record the hall sensor investigation and the
++ working build procedure
++
++The hall sensors were never broken: the mxm1120 driver deliberately wrote only
++the mode bit of the operation mode register, so the part never started
++converting and every sample was refused (bbk_hall_data reported the -2000
++failure value).  Setting the factory's START bits (0x40 | 0x09) makes both
++sensors report valid, position dependent samples - verified on the device.
++
++The patch is kept unmerged, though: with valid samples the camera service
++raises the front camera only to MID and stops there, which is exactly the
++'stops half way' behaviour that made the sensors idle in the first place.
++
++Also record that kernels must be built with build_eebbk_clang11.sh: the two
++kernels built with ad-hoc make invocations did not boot, while a build from a
++fresh out directory with a pristine config does.  h130_debug.config is the
++configuration with CONFIG_BBK_DEBUG_BRINGUP=y that the running debug image
++uses.
++
++Signed-off-by: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
