+Subject: [PATCH 70/70] tree: track the firmware blobs the build needs but
+ .gitignore hid
+
+A worktree check (check out the vendor-import commit, apply patch_final, compare
+with the final tree) showed 22 paths that the patches could not reproduce.  The
+reason is that the kernel's own .gitignore ignores "*.bin" under firmware/ and
+the focaltech driver's firmware blobs, so they were never committed:
+
+* firmware/aw882xx_{spk,rcv}_reg_{l,r}.bin -- required by
+  CONFIG_EXTRA_FIRMWARE, without them a fresh clone builds a kernel with no
+  amplifier register tables (i.e. no sound);
+* drivers/input/touchscreen/focaltech_touch/include/{firmware,pramboot}/*.i --
+  the touch controller firmware blobs;
+* KernelSU/.gitattributes, kernel/.clang-format, kernel/.clangd.example and
+  kernel/.vscode/* -- upstream KernelSU files needed to keep the vendored copy
+  complete.
+
+Force-added with `git add -f`; the copies under
+techpack/audio/asoc/codecs/awinic/firmware/ were already tracked.
+
